Chopped forests grow back again.

1) A room that had been logged only recovered if it was chopped completely
   bare, and even then stalled one log short of full forever.
   - Rooms chopped partway recovered nothing at all.

2) Reforestation now works the way fishing always has.
   - Any room with logs taken from it recovers, a log at a time.
   - Both run on the same pulse at the same rate, so a stripped grove takes
     about as long to come back as a fished-out pool.

